summary:
  The "no titles" pin is written as the address playback is heard on, so a
  relayed station pins a loopback while every road that lifts the pin looks
  for the station — and the five-minute recheck never fires.

history:
  The pin's own recheck arrived 2026-09-06 with the fix for issue #10, and
  it was born half dead: the pin was stored raw from playMusic.source while
  the recheck compared it through _icyStreamTarget. Those two agree only
  when nothing relays. An Ogg or FLAC station — or an mp3 the rescue put
  behind the relay, which the very same commit taught to poll for titles —
  plays from 127.0.0.1, so the comparison failed on its first line and the
  pin stood for the whole play. Found 2026-09-08, before release.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
              var queryUrl = _icyStreamTarget(playMusic.source);

replace:
              var queryUrl = playMusic.source.toString();

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_the_no_titles_pin_names_the_station_not_the_transport.
  Line-neutral, as main.qml's ratchet requires.
